@preamble use("math/ffi")
floor
Returns the largest integer less than or equal to x.

floor(x)

floor(3.7)     # 3
floor(-2.3)    # -3
===
ceil
Returns the smallest integer greater than or equal to x.

ceil(x)

ceil(3.2)     # 4
ceil(-2.7)    # -2
===
modulo
Returns the Euclidean remainder of integral a divided by non-zero integral b.
This provider operation faults for non-integral operands or division by zero.

modulo(a, b)

modulo(10, 3)    # 1
modulo(7, 2)     # 1
===
sin
Returns the sine of x, where x is in radians, using host float64 mathematics.
The returned float value crosses back into Aiki as an ordinary exact rational
representation of that float result.

sin(x)

sin(0)           # 0
sin(3.14159/2)   # approximately 1
===
cos
Returns the cosine of x, where x is in radians, using host float64 mathematics.
The returned float value crosses back into Aiki as an ordinary exact rational
representation of that float result.

cos(x)

cos(0)           # 1
cos(3.14159)     # approximately -1
===
sqrt
Returns the square root of x using host float64 mathematics. Negative inputs
fault. The returned float value crosses back into Aiki as an ordinary exact
rational representation of that float result.
Faults on negative input.

sqrt(x)

sqrt(4)     # 2
sqrt(2)     # approximately 1.414
